-### PART 3 — BRAND & TYPOGRAPHY GUIDE
-
-#### Color Palette
-
-| Role | Color | Hex | Usage |
-|---|---|---|---|
-| Primary dark | Charcoal | `#1C1F22` | Backgrounds for manifesto/pledge sections, primary body text on white |
-| Primary light | Off-white | `#F5F4F0` | Page background, negative space, card backgrounds |
-| Structural | Ocean Blue | `#1E4B6B` | Section headers, subheads, chart-adjacent graphic elements, links |
-| Accent (primary) | Amber | `#E8912D` | CTAs, price callouts, leader lines/labels in technical diagrams, stretch-goal milestones hit |
-| Accent (secondary) | Teal | `#2F9C95` | Used sparingly for "open source" specific tags (GitHub icon accents, license badges) — keeps amber reserved for money/price/action |
-| Alert / Risk | Muted Red | `#B33A3A` | Risk matrix high-severity dots only — not used decoratively elsewhere |
-| Success / Checkmark | Deep Green | `#3B7A57` | Tier comparison checkmarks only |
-
-**Usage rule:** Amber and teal should never both appear as primary accents in the same section — pick one per section based on whether the section is about *money/action* (amber) or *openness/technical* (teal). This keeps the palette from feeling busy.
-
-#### Logo Concept
-
-A compass rose where the four cardinal points are rendered as **open brackets** (`< >` style, code-bracket aesthetic) instead of traditional arrowheads — north point extended slightly longer, in the style of a real marine compass rose, but constructed entirely from bracket/caret geometry so it reads as "open-source" at a glance to a technical audience while still reading as "compass" at a glance to a boater. Rendered in a single color (charcoal on light backgrounds, off-white on dark/manifesto backgrounds) — no gradient, no drop shadow, should work as a 1-color engraving or embroidery patch.
-
-Alternative secondary mark: the same compass rose with the north point terminating in an open (unlocked) padlock shackle shape — reserve this variant specifically for use near the Pledge section and licensing/GitHub callouts, not as the primary logo.
-
-#### Typography
-
-| Use | Typeface | Notes |
-|---|---|---|
-| Headlines, section titles, CTAs | **Montserrat** (Bold/ExtraBold) | Upper-case for top-level headers, sentence case for subheads |
-| Long-form story copy (Problem/Solution/Founder statement body) | **Source Serif** (Regular/Italic for pull-quotes) | Generous line-height (1.6+), max line length ~70 characters for readability |
-| Spec sheets, labels, technical diagram callouts, pledge block, price tables, GitHub file names | **JetBrains Mono** (Regular/Medium) | Lowercase preferred for labels to feel like real filenames/terminal output rather than marketing type |
-
-**Rule of thumb:** If it's a claim or a feeling → Source Serif. If it's a fact, a spec, or a number → JetBrains Mono. If it's a directive (headline, button, section title) → Montserrat.
